    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d826">

                <pb facs="0910" n="1744" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 600.119/1259</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-31T19:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 31, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 1, 9.35
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1761. War Trade Board [from Chadbourne]:</p>
                <p>233. Understand United States bunker rules do not apply to boats sailing between
                    Spain and Cuba not touching at any port in the United States or its possessions
                    but do not know whether or not the Republic of Cuba has issued bunker rules of
                    its own by agreement with United States. Please inform so that we may advise
                    consuls. Chadbourne.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
